6. INTRODUCTION

Column-average Dry Mole Fractions (DMF) reported in this file were
acquired using a Fourier Transform Spectrometer (FTS) located at the
Wisconsin Tall Tower (WLEF) site (45.945 deg N, 90.273 deg W, 442 m above
sea level).  Direct solar spectra were acquired in the near-infrared
spectral region.  These spectra were used to retrieve column abundances
of CO2, CH4, CO, H2O, HDO, O2, and other atmospheric gases.

More information about the TCCON network can be found on the TCCON wiki:

   https://tccon-wiki.caltech.edu

about the Park Fall FTS container specifically can be found at:

   https://tccon-wiki.caltech.edu/Main/ParkFalls

(For a username and password to the tccon-wiki, please email coleen@caltech.edu.)

See also, TCCON papers:

Washenfelder, R.A., G.C. Toon, J-F. Blavier, Z. Yang, N.T. Allen
P.O. Wennberg, S.A. Vay, D.M. Matross, and B.C. Daube, 2006.  Carbon
dioxide column abundances at the Wisconsin Tall Tower site, Journal of
Geophysical Research, 2006, 111, doi:10.1029/2006JD007154.

